{"id":"mahabharata-7-028","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":28,"title":"अष्टाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 28 · Arjuna kills Bhagadatta","summary":{"en":"Arjuna and Bhagadatta fight, and Bhagadatta hurls the Vaishnava weapon, which Krishna takes on his own chest where it becomes a garland. Arjuna then kills the king of Pragjyotisha and his elephant.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ ಮತ್ತು ಭಗದತ್ತರ ಯುದ್ಧ; ಭಗದತ್ತ ವೈಷ್ಣವಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಎಸೆಯಲು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅದನ್ನು ತನ್ನ ಎದೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸಿ ಮಾಲೆಯಾಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನ ಪ್ರಾಗ್ಜ್ಯೋತಿಷ ರಾಜನನ್ನೂ ಅವನ ಆನೆಯನ್ನೂ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन और भगदत्त लड़ते हैं, भगदत्त वैष्णवास्त्र फेंकता है जिसे कृष्ण अपनी छाती पर लेते हैं और वह माला बन जाता है। अर्जुन फिर प्राग्ज्योतिष के राजा और उसके हाथी को मार देते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు, భగదత్తుడు పోరాడతారు; భగదత్తుడు వైష్ణవాస్త్రం ప్రయోగించగా కృష్ణుడు దాన్ని తన వక్షస్థలంపై స్వీకరించి మాలగా మారుస్తాడు. అర్జునుడు ప్రాగ్జ్యోతిష రాజును, అతని ఏనుగును చంపుతాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனனும் பகதத்தனும் போரிட, பகதத்தன் வைஷ்ணவாஸ்திரத்தை ஏவ, கண்ணன் அதைத் தன் மார்பில் ஏற்று மாலையாக்குகிறார். அர்ஜுனன் பிராக்ஜோதிஷ மன்னனையும் அவன் யானையையும் கொல்கிறான்.","ml":"അർജുനനും ഭഗദത്തനും തമ്മിൽ പൊരുതുന്നു; ഭഗദത്തൻ വൈഷ്ണവാസ്ത്രം പ്രയോഗിക്കുന്നു, അത് കൃഷ്ണൻ സ്വന്തം മാറിൽ ഏറ്റുവാങ്ങി മാലയാക്കി മാറ്റുന്നു. പിന്നീട് അർജുനൻ പ്രാഗ്ജ്യോതിഷ രാജാവിനെയും അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ആനയെയും വധിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.28; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संशप्तकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Samshaptakavadha Parva (Slaying of the Samshaptakas)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा क्रुद्धः किमकरोद्भगदत्तस्य पाण्डवः ।\nप्राग्ज्योतिषो वा पार्थस्य तन्मे शंस यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged like that, what did the Pandava do to Bhagadatta, or what did Pragjyotisha do to Partha? Tell me exactly as it was."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषेण संसक्तावुभौ दाशार्हपाण्डवौ ।\nमृत्योरिवान्तिकं प्राप्तौ सर्वभूतानि मेनिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Dasharha and the Pandava, locked in fight with Pragjyotisha, were thought by all beings to have come to Death's very door."}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा हि शरवर्षाणि पातयत्यनिशं प्रभो ।\nभगदत्तो गजस्कन्धात्कृष्णयोः स्यन्दनस्थयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Bhagadatta, from the elephant's neck, was ceaselessly pouring showers of arrows on the two Krishnas in their chariot."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ कार्ष्णायसैर्बाणैः पूर्णकार्मुकनिःसृतैः ।\nअविध्यद्देवकीपुत्रं हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With dark iron arrows sped from a fully drawn bow, gold-feathered and sharpened on stone, he pierced Devaki's son."}},{"n":5,"text":"अग्निस्पर्शसमास्तीक्ष्णा भगदत्तेन चोदिताः ।\nनिर्भिद्य देवकीपुत्रं क्षितिं जग्मुः शरास्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sharp as the touch of fire, those arrows loosed by Bhagadatta pierced Devaki's son and went down into the earth."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्य पार्थो धनुश्छित्त्वा शरावापं निहत्य च ।\nलाडयन्निव राजानं भगदत्तमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha cut down his bow, destroyed his quiver, and fought King Bhagadatta almost as if playing with him."}},{"n":7,"text":"सोऽर्करश्मिनिभांस्तीक्ष्णांस्तोमरान्वै चतुर्दश ।\nप्रेरयत्सव्यसाची तांस्त्रिधैकैकमथाच्छिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta hurled fourteen sharp lances bright as sunbeams; Savyasachi cut each of them into three."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो नागस्य तद्वर्म व्यधमत्पाकशासनिः ।\nशरजालेन स बभौ व्यभ्रः पर्वतराडिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra's son shattered the elephant's armor with a net of arrows, and the elephant, stripped, looked like the king of mountains without clouds."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः प्राग्ज्योतिषः शक्तिं हेमदण्डामयस्मयीम् ।\nव्यसृजद्वासुदेवाय द्विधा तामर्जुनोऽच्छिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pragjyotisha then hurled at Vasudeva an iron spear with a golden shaft, and Arjuna cut it in two."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततश्छत्रं ध्वजं चैव छित्त्वा राज्ञोऽर्जुनः शरैः ।\nविव्याध दशभिस्तूर्णमुत्स्मयन्पर्वताधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna cut down the king's umbrella and banner with arrows and quickly pierced the mountain lord with ten more, smiling."}},{"n":11,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धोऽर्जुनशरैः सुपुङ्खैः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ।\nभगदत्तस्ततः क्रुद्धः पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by Arjuna's fine-feathered, heron-winged arrows, Bhagadatta grew angry at the great-souled Pandava."}},{"n":12,"text":"व्यसृजत्तोमरान्मूर्ध्नि श्वेताश्वस्योन्ननाद च ।\nतैरर्जुनस्य समरे किरीटं परिवर्तितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He hurled lances at the head of the white-horsed Arjuna and roared, and with them Arjuna's diadem was turned in the battle."}},{"n":13,"text":"परिवृत्तं किरीटं तं यमयन्नेव फल्गुनः ।\nसुदृष्टः क्रियतां लोक इति राजानमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Setting that turned diadem straight, Phalguna said to the king: \"Take a good look at the world now.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु संक्रुद्धः शरवर्षेण पाण्डवम् ।\nअभ्यवर्षत्सगोविन्दं धनुरादाय भास्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, Bhagadatta, furious, took up a shining bow and showered arrows on the Pandava and Govinda."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्य पार्थो धनुश्छित्त्वा तूणीरान्संनिकृत्य च ।\nत्वरमाणो द्विसप्तत्या सर्वमर्मस्वताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha cut down his bow, cut his quivers to pieces, and swiftly struck him with seventy-two arrows in all his vital parts."}},{"n":16,"text":"विद्धस्तथाप्यव्यथितो वैष्णवास्त्रमुदीरयन् ।\nअभिमन्त्र्याङ्कुशं क्रुद्धो व्यसृजत्पाण्डवोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced, yet unshaken, he raised the Vaishnava weapon; in anger he consecrated his goad with a mantra and hurled it at the Pandava's chest."}},{"n":17,"text":"विसृष्टं भगदत्तेन तदस्त्रं सर्वघातकम् ।\nउरसा प्रतिजग्राह पार्थं संछाद्य केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That weapon, hurled by Bhagadatta, which kills everything, Keshava received on his own chest, covering Partha."}},{"n":18,"text":"वैजयन्त्यभवन्माला तदस्त्रं केशवोरसि ।\nततोऽर्जुनः क्लान्तमनाः केशवं प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"On Keshava's chest the weapon became a Vaijayanti garland. Then Arjuna, troubled in mind, said to Keshava:"}},{"n":19,"text":"अयुध्यमानस्तुरगान्संयन्तास्मि जनार्दन ।\nइत्युक्त्वा पुण्डरीकाक्ष प्रतिज्ञां स्वां न रक्षसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Janardana, you said you would only hold the horses and not fight; lotus-eyed one, having said so, you do not keep your pledge.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"यद्यहं व्यसनी वा स्यामशक्तो वा निवारणे ।\nततस्त्वयैवं कार्यं स्यान्न तु कार्यं मयि स्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I were in trouble, or unable to ward it off, then you would have to do this; but not while I stand here.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"सबाणः सधनुश्चाहं ससुरासुरमानवान् ।\nशक्तो लोकानिमाञ्जेतुं तच्चापि विदितं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With my bow and arrows I can conquer these worlds, with gods, demons and men; and you know that too.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनं वासुदेवः प्रत्युवाचार्थवद्वचः ।\nशृणु गुह्यमिदं पार्थ यथा वृत्तं पुरानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vasudeva answered Arjuna with meaningful words: \"Listen, sinless Partha, to this secret, as it happened long ago.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"चतुर्मूर्तिरहं शश्वल्लोकत्राणार्थमुद्यतः ।\nआत्मानं प्रविभज्येह लोकानां हितमादधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am four-formed, always engaged in protecting the worlds. Dividing myself here, I work for the good of the worlds.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एका मूर्तिस्तपश्चर्यां कुरुते मे भुवि स्थिता ।\nअपरा पश्यति जगत्कुर्वाणं साध्वसाधुनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One form of mine stays on earth and practices austerity; another watches the world, seeing the good and bad that people do.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अपरा कुरुते कर्म मानुषं लोकमाश्रिता ।\nशेते चतुर्थी त्वपरा निद्रां वर्षसहस्रिकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A third form acts in the human world, doing deeds; the fourth sleeps a sleep of a thousand years.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"यासौ वर्षसहस्रान्ते मूर्तिरुत्तिष्ठते मम ।\nवरार्हेभ्यो वराञ्श्रेष्ठांस्तस्मिन्काले ददाति सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The form of mine that rises at the end of the thousand years gives, in that time, the best of boons to those who deserve them.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तं तु कालमनुप्राप्तं विदित्वा पृथिवी तदा ।\nप्रायाचत वरं यं मां नरकार्थाय तं शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knowing that time had come, Earth then asked of me a boon, for Naraka's sake; hear what it was.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"देवानामसुराणां च अवध्यस्तनयोऽस्तु मे ।\nउपेतो वैष्णवास्त्रेण तन्मे त्वं दातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Let my son be unslayable by gods and demons, and endowed with the Vaishnava weapon; you should give me that.'\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एवं वरमहं श्रुत्वा जगत्यास्तनये तदा ।\nअमोघमस्त्रमददं वैष्णवं तदहं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing that boon asked by Earth for her son, I then gave her the Vaishnava weapon, which never fails.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"अवोचं चैतदस्त्रं वै ह्यमोघं भवतु क्षमे ।\nनरकस्याभिरक्षार्थं नैनं कश्चिद्वधिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I said: 'Earth, let this weapon be unfailing; to protect Naraka, no one will kill him.'\""}},{"n":31,"text":"अनेनास्त्रेण ते गुप्तः सुतः परबलार्दनः ।\nभविष्यति दुराधर्षः सर्वलोकेषु सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Guarded by this weapon, your son, tormentor of enemy armies, will be unassailable in all the worlds, always.'\""}},{"n":32,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा गता देवी कृतकामा मनस्विनी ।\nस चाप्यासीद्दुराधर्षो नरकः शत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Saying 'So be it', the proud goddess, her wish fulfilled, went away; and Naraka became unassailable, a scorcher of enemies.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्मात्प्राग्ज्योतिषं प्राप्तं तदस्त्रं पार्थ मामकम् ।\nनास्यावध्योऽस्ति लोकेषु सेन्द्ररुद्रेषु मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That weapon of mine, Partha, passed to Pragjyotisha; no one in the worlds, even with Indra and Rudra, is able to kill him while he has it, O sir.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"तन्मया त्वत्कृतेनैतदन्यथा व्यपनाशितम् ।\nवियुक्तं परमास्त्रेण जहि पार्थ महासुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But for your sake I have made it fail; it has left him. Now kill that great Asura, Partha, who is released from the supreme weapon,\""}},{"n":35,"text":"वैरिणं युधि दुर्धर्षं भगदत्तं सुरद्विषम् ।\nयथाहं जघ्निवान्पूर्वं हितार्थं नरकं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhagadatta, the hard-to-beat enemy of the gods, as once for their good I killed Naraka.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततः पार्थः केशवेन महात्मना ।\nभगदत्तं शितैर्बाणैः सहसा समवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by great-souled Keshava, Partha suddenly covered Bhagadatta with sharp arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः पार्थो महाबाहुरसंभ्रान्तो महामनाः ।\nकुम्भयोरन्तरे नागं नाराचेन समार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed, steady, high-minded Partha struck the elephant between its temples with an iron arrow."}},{"n":38,"text":"समासाद्य तु तं नागं बाणो वज्र इवाचलम् ।\nअभ्यगात्सह पुङ्खेन वल्मीकमिव पन्नगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That arrow, reaching the elephant like a thunderbolt a mountain, went in with its feathers, like a serpent into an anthill."}},{"n":39,"text":"स तु विष्टभ्य गात्राणि दन्ताभ्यामवनिं ययौ ।\nनदन्नार्तस्वरं प्राणानुत्ससर्ज महाद्विपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stiffening its limbs, the elephant sank to the ground on its tusks, crying in pain, and gave up its life, that great beast."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततश्चन्द्रार्धबिम्बेन शरेण नतपर्वणा ।\nबिभेद हृदयं राज्ञो भगदत्तस्य पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava pierced the heart of King Bhagadatta with a half-moon-headed, bent-jointed arrow."}},{"n":41,"text":"स भिन्नहृदयो राजा भगदत्तः किरीटिना ।\nशरासनं शरांश्चैव गतासुः प्रमुमोच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"His heart pierced by the diadem-wearer, King Bhagadatta, lifeless, let go of his bow and arrows."}},{"n":42,"text":"शिरसस्तस्य विभ्रष्टः पपात च वराङ्कुशः ।\nनालताडनविभ्रष्टं पलाशं नलिनादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His fine goad slipped from his head and fell, like a palasha leaf, loosened by its stalk's shaking, falling from a lotus."}},{"n":43,"text":"स हेममाली तपनीयभाण्डा-\nत्पपात नागाद्गिरिसंनिकाशात् ।\nसुपुष्पितो मारुतवेगरुग्णो\nमहीधराग्रादिव कर्णिकारः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wearing a golden garland, he fell from the golden-adorned elephant like a mountain, as a flowering karnikara tree, broken by the wind's force, falls from a mountain's peak."}},{"n":44,"text":"निहत्य तं नरपतिमिन्द्रविक्रमं\nसखायमिन्द्रस्य तथैन्द्रिराहवे ।\nततोऽपरांस्तव जयकाङ्क्षिणो नरा-\nन्बभञ्ज वायुर्बलवान्द्रुमानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed that king, who had Indra's might and was Indra's friend, Indra's son then broke other men of yours eager for victory, as the strong wind breaks trees."}}]}]}